    why: "A value stored with \"launchsafe-firewall vault add\" is always a credential. The firewall keeps its fingerprints (never the value) and looks for them in everything leaving, also base64, base32, hex, URL and DNS-label encoded. Sending it anywhere the person did not bind that secret to (\"vault allow\") is denied, whatever dataAllowHosts and sendAllowHosts say, because the per-secret binding is the narrower statement. This catches a value that reached the agent some other way, such as a .env file it read. If the vault index is not signed by your approval key, no destination counts as bound.",
