    why: "The agent writes vault://<name> where a secret's value would go, and the firewall puts the value in only for destinations the person bound that secret to (\"vault allow\": a host, an MCP server and tool, or a command line for run). A reference to no stored secret (a typo) is denied so the reference text never goes out as if it were a value; so is a destination the secret is not bound to, a value inside a URL without --allow-in-url (URLs end up in logs and proxies), and any reference while the vault index is not signed by your approval key. Nothing is read from the store for a denied action.",
